      <data key="d2">cb-0237</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WORLD WAR I&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"World War I is the conflict during which Admiral Creswell prepared the Australian naval fleet, marking a significant period in his career."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0237</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEW ZEALAND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"New Zealand is mentioned in relation to the Robert Falla Memorial Award, honoring a renowned New Zealand ornithologist."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0237</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ORNITHOLOGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ornithology is the field of study that Admiral Creswell contributed to, receiving recognition for his work."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0237</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SEABIRD MIGRATION PATTERNS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Seabird Migration Patterns is the subject of Admiral Creswell's groundbreaking research, earning him recognition from the scientific community."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0237</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AUSTRALIAN NAVY&quot;">
      <data key="d2">cb-0237</data>
      <data key="d1">"William Rooke Creswell played a significant role in the development of the Australian Navy, making him a pioneering figure in its history."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
